course: dictionary
lesson: 7917
title: Raw: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Raw means not cooked, or still in its natural state. «Raw eggs, raw flour and uncooked meat can carry germs, so they are eaten only when properly cooked.» Here raw and uncooked mean the same thing, and the words around it tell you so.
explain: Raw can change meaning with the words next to it. In «raw materials», raw means not yet made into something, so wood, oil and metal ore are raw materials before factories turn them into products. In «a raw deal», raw means unfair. The clue is always the word that comes with raw.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Mutations are the raw material of evolution» still makes sense with starting material in place of raw material. If the sentence makes no sense, try another meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Raw» means not cooked: raw chicken must be cooked properly before you eat it.
fact: «Raw materials» are things in their natural state, like wood, oil or metal ore, before they are made into something.
fact: «Raw» can also mean red and sore, as if rubbed, or cold and damp, as in raw weather.
fact: Raw meat can carry germs, so wash your hands after touching it.
exercise: «Raw eggs, raw flour and uncooked meat can carry germs, so they are eaten only when properly cooked.» In this sentence, what does raw mean? | *Not cooked | Red and sore | Very fresh and tasty | Cold and wet
exercise: «Mutations are the raw material of evolution.» What does raw material mean here? | A feeling of strong sadness | *The starting stuff that other things are made from | A material that is cooked and ready to eat
exercise: Raw skin is red and sore, as if rubbed. What does raw skin look like? | Dry and flaky | *Red and sore | Cooked and golden | Smooth and cool
test: «Undercooked chicken, still pink inside, and unwashed hands after touching raw meat can give people food poisoning.» Which action keeps you safe after touching raw meat? | Leave the meat out to warm up | Lick your fingers | *Wash your hands | Eat something straight away
test: Which sentence uses raw to mean strong and painful? | The wood was cut into raw planks | The bread was raw in the middle | The fish was raw and ready to cook | *The loss left her with raw feelings of grief
exam: Sam says «raw» always means red and sore. Why is he wrong? | Raw is a number | *Raw has several meanings, so the context shows which one is meant | Raw is only used for food | Raw always means cooked
